Write the weekly memo for the user (meeting owner) to send to the team, from the notes file /private/tmp/hirearchy-p2/R1-1793275867/notes/2026-11-09.md (read it by absolute path; never edit anything there). Write it to lead/writer/work/2026-11-09-memo.md. Use only what is in that file; no attendee list, no next-meeting date, nothing from other files.

Hints from past client feedback:
- Line 1 of the memo must be exactly one line starting 'Summary:' (one-line summary of the meeting). Then the '## Decisions' section, then the action items table, then a final '## Unclear' heading (last).
- A statement that something stays as it is (nobody has to do anything) gets no table row.
- A relative deadline like 'by Friday' becomes an ISO date when the notes make it clear: check weekday against the meeting date (Monday 9 November 2026) with the calendar. Prose commitments ('X said he would/he'd ...') are rows. A commitment with no date gets Due 'none'.
- Owner names exactly as written in the notes. Facts that are not decisions are not listed under Decisions.
- Anything unclear goes under Unclear instead of being guessed.

## Acceptance criteria
- C1: The memo is markdown and has at most 400 words as counted by read.
- C2: The memo has a Decisions section listing every decision made in the named notes file, and nothing from other files.
- C3: The action items are a markdown table with exactly the columns Owner | Action | Due.
- C4: Every commitment in the notes is a row of the table, both those labelled ACTION and those stated in prose, such as someone saying they would do something.
- C5: Each Due value is an ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD). A relative deadline such as 'by Friday' is turned into a date only when the notes make the date clear; if the notes give no date, Due is 'none'.
- C6: Each Owner value uses the name exactly as written in the notes.
- C7: Every statement in the memo is traceable to the notes file, and anything unclear (no owner, an unconfirmed decision) is listed under a final heading 'Unclear' instead of being guessed.
- C9: The memo starts with a one-line 'Summary:' of the meeting, followed by the Decisions section, then the action items table.
- C10: A statement that something stays as it is, where nobody has to do anything, is not an action item and gets no row in the table.
Deliverable: named 2026-11-09-memo.md; markdown; at most 400 words.

